usbip: reclaim busid entries the rebind path never sees

del_match_busid() only clears an entry whose status is STUB_BUSID_OTHER.  For
anything else it marks the entry STUB_BUSID_REMOV and keeps the name, because
stub_disconnect() looks the entry up and BUG()s when it cannot find it.

Reclaim used to happen at the end of stub_disconnect(), for every entry that was
not STUB_BUSID_ALLOC: it set the status to OTHER and called del_match_busid().
Two 2018 commits reshaped that:

  1e180f167d4e  usbip: usbip_host: delete device from busid_table after rebind
                put the deletion in rebind_store(), after device_attach()
                succeeds, because "Device is left in the busid_table after
                unbind and rebind".

  22d4a89efe86  usbip: usbip_host: run rebind from exit when module is removed
                removed the deletion from stub_disconnect(), because the module
                exit rescan hands devices back to their drivers by looking
                their names up in that table.

What remains is a single reclaim point, rebind_store(), and it only runs when
userspace writes "rebind".  A bare "del" - which is exactly what a udev helper
does when a device goes away - never reaches it, so the entry keeps its name and
its slot for the lifetime of the module.  add_match_busid() then returns success
for that busid without re-arming it, so the next "usbip bind" reports success
while stub_probe() keeps skipping the device, and every bind that ends this way
burns another slot until the table is full and all further binds fail with
-ENOMEM.

This patch extends the reclaim to the paths commit 1e180f167d4e left out, keyed
on one invariant: an entry whose sdev is NULL has no device attached, so no
stub_disconnect() is running or can start for it, which is what makes clearing
the name safe there.  While a device is claimed the name has to stay.

  - del_match_busid(): clear when the status is STUB_BUSID_OTHER *or* sdev is
    NULL, instead of handling OTHER only.  Covers an idle STUB_BUSID_ADDED entry
    whose authorization was revoked, and a STUB_BUSID_REMOV entry whose
    disconnect has already finished.

  - add_match_busid(): re-arm an orphaned entry (sdev NULL, status OTHER or
    REMOV) to STUB_BUSID_ADDED, so a bind that follows a half finished unbind
    exports the device again instead of returning success and doing nothing.

Behaviour for a live session is unchanged: a claimed device keeps its name, the
status transitions are the same as before, and the new clearing only happens
where no stub_disconnect() can follow.

Checked with -fsyntax-only against the rkr8 sources in this SDK; the runtime
checks to run on the board are listed in patches/kernel/README.md.
diff --git a/drivers/usb/usbip/stub_main.c b/drivers/usb/usbip/stub_main.c
index c1c0bbc9f8b1..48fb523f4c8f 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/usbip/stub_main.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/usbip/stub_main.c
@@ -89,12 +89,21 @@ void put_busid_priv(struct bus_id_priv *bid)
 
 static int add_match_busid(char *busid)
 {
+	int idx;
 	int i;
 	int ret = -1;
 
 	spin_lock(&busid_table_lock);
-	/* already registered? */
-	if (get_busid_idx(busid) >= 0) {
+	idx = get_busid_idx(busid);
+	if (idx >= 0) {
+		/* already registered, reuse the entry if it is orphaned */
+		spin_lock(&busid_table[idx].busid_lock);
+		if (!busid_table[idx].sdev &&
+		    (busid_table[idx].status == STUB_BUSID_OTHER ||
+		     busid_table[idx].status == STUB_BUSID_REMOV))
+			busid_table[idx].status = STUB_BUSID_ADDED;
+		spin_unlock(&busid_table[idx].busid_lock);
+
 		ret = 0;
 		goto out;
 	}
@@ -134,12 +143,20 @@ int del_match_busid(char *busid)
 
 	spin_lock(&busid_table[idx].busid_lock);
 
-	if (busid_table[idx].status == STUB_BUSID_OTHER)
+	/*
+	 * Drop the entry when nothing owns it.  The name has to survive while a
+	 * device is claimed, because stub_disconnect() looks it up, and until
+	 * that disconnect has finished, which is where sdev becomes NULL.  Past
+	 * that point the entry is orphaned and this is the only path that can
+	 * reclaim it.
+	 */
+	if (busid_table[idx].status == STUB_BUSID_OTHER ||
+	    !busid_table[idx].sdev) {
 		memset(busid_table[idx].name, 0, BUSID_SIZE);
-
-	if ((busid_table[idx].status != STUB_BUSID_OTHER) &&
-	    (busid_table[idx].status != STUB_BUSID_ADDED))
+		busid_table[idx].status = STUB_BUSID_OTHER;
+	} else {
 		busid_table[idx].status = STUB_BUSID_REMOV;
+	}
 
 	spin_unlock(&busid_table[idx].busid_lock);
 out:
